      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: error-structure\n",
        "blank_by_file = json.load(open(\"results/pair_agreement.json\"))[\"blank_share_by_file\"]\n",
        "pa100 = json.load(open(\"results/pair_agreement.json\"))[\"finder_100k.csv\"][\"fields\"]\n",
        "FIELD_LABELS = [(\"first_name\", \"First name\"), (\"middle_initial\", \"Middle initial\"), (\"last_name\", \"Last name\"),\n",
        "                (\"date_of_birth\", \"Date of birth\"), (\"sex\", \"Sex\"), (\"race_ethnicity\", \"Race/ethnicity\"),\n",
        "                (\"street_number\", \"Street number\"), (\"street_name\", \"Street name\"), (\"unit_number\", \"Unit number\"),\n",
        "                (\"city\", \"City\"), (\"state\", \"State\"), (\"zipcode\", \"ZIP code\"), (\"ssn\", \"SSN\")]\n",
        "ADDRESS = {\"street_number\", \"street_name\", \"unit_number\", \"city\", \"state\", \"zipcode\"}\n",
        "def set_rate(file_kind, field):\n",
        "    if field == \"ssn\":\n",
        "        return no[file_kind][\"ssn_missing\"]\n",
        "    if field in ADDRESS:\n",
        "        return no[file_kind][\"address_missing\"]\n",
        "    return 0.01  # pseudopeople's default leave_blank probability for every other field\n",
        "def blank_cell(fname, kind, field):\n",
        "    return f\"{pct(blank_by_file[fname][field], 1)} ({pct(set_rate(kind, field), 0)})\"\n",
        "errors_100k_max_diff_pp = f\"{100 * max(abs(pa[f][k] - pa100[f][k]) for f in pa for k in ('agree_when_both_present', 'blank_on_either_side')):.1f}\"\n",
        "unit_blank_reg = pct(blank_by_file[\"registry.csv\"][\"unit_number\"], 0)"
      ],
      "id": "error-structure",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "@tbl-errors gives the error structure field by field: the share of values that are blank in the registry and in the larger finder file, against the blanking rate set for each, and, among the `{python} overlap_500k_pairs` true pairs, the share of pairs whose two records agree exactly when both have a value and the share with a blank on either side. The smaller finder file matches the larger on every figure in the table to within `{python} errors_100k_max_diff_pp` percentage points.\n",
        "\n",
        "SSNs are blank in `{python} finder_ssn_missing` of finder records, the rate FCDS specified, and in `{python} registry_ssn_missing` of registry records against a specified `{python} cfg_registry_ssn_missing`; the excess is structural, since `{python} pop_ssn_never` of the people in the registry pool never held an SSN in the source population. Of the SSNs present in the larger finder file, `{python} err_ssn_transposed` carry two adjacent digits swapped, and where a true pair has an SSN on both sides the two agree in `{python} agree_ssn_500k` of pairs.\n",
        "\n",
        "Names and dates of birth disagree more often than SSNs do. Among true pairs with both values present, first names agree in `{python} agree_first_name_500k` of pairs, last names in `{python} agree_last_name_500k` and dates of birth in `{python} agree_dob_500k`, and each of these fields is blank on one side in about `{python} blank_first_name_500k` of pairs. Taken together, `{python} name_dob_all_agree_500k` of true pairs agree exactly on first name, last name and date of birth, and `{python} ssn_usable_500k` have an SSN on both sides that agrees; these two shares bound what exact-match rules can find in @sec-difficulty. Address fields agree in `{python} agree_street_name_500k` of pairs with both present and are blank on one side in `{python} blank_street_name_500k`; the unit number is blank for `{python} unit_blank_reg` of registry records, because most addresses have none, and street numbers are blank above their set rates because some source addresses carry none."
